      "text": "Let's represent the two numbers as y and x. Based on the given information, we can create the following equations:\n\n1) For both numbers: x + y = 6\n2) For their squares: x² - y² = 12 (Equation 1: Using the difference of squares)\n\nWe can utilize Strategy 2: Using the difference of squares to factorise Equation 1:\n\n(x - y) (x + y) = 12\n\nUsing the value of x + y given in Equation 1:\n(x - y) (6) = 12\n(x - y) = 12 / (x + y)\n(x - y) = 12 / 6\n(x - y) = 2\n\nTherefore, the positive difference between the two numbers is equal to 2.",
